[{:db/id 17592186078496 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-128c4108-f47c-515a-aaac-ed93eb92e39c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-128c4108-f47c-515a-aaac-ed93eb92e39c" :question/id #uuid "128c4108-f47c-515a-aaac-ed93eb92e39c" :question/math-academy-id "q-64708" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(t)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-10y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-10{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -2)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-5$ or $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-5t}$ and ${e}^{2t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-3{e}^{-5t}+2{e}^{-2t}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f1bdcac-c8f7-5ea7-bb80-b176a1307c71"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f1bdcac-c8f7-5ea7-bb80-b176a1307c71" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f1bdcac-c8f7-5ea7-bb80-b176a1307c71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a3822e6-4ea3-5bd8-88d6-1f35c1d51f37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a3822e6-4ea3-5bd8-88d6-1f35c1d51f37" "answer-e0c2bf7c-2f4c-5e0e-8a59-5fd6f0e6f6d1" "answer-463b0c74-3f5f-5ede-984f-20e81cf9dab4" "answer-3bda799f-2dc1-508a-b332-a2dc15ad6469" "answer-bbd12f7d-a1de-5498-8a07-57a3b71dfca4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a3822e6-4ea3-5bd8-88d6-1f35c1d51f37" :answer/id #uuid "6a3822e6-4ea3-5bd8-88d6-1f35c1d51f37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{e}^{-5t}+2{e}^{-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0c2bf7c-2f4c-5e0e-8a59-5fd6f0e6f6d1" :answer/id #uuid "e0c2bf7c-2f4c-5e0e-8a59-5fd6f0e6f6d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-463b0c74-3f5f-5ede-984f-20e81cf9dab4" :answer/id #uuid "463b0c74-3f5f-5ede-984f-20e81cf9dab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-5t}+6{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bda799f-2dc1-508a-b332-a2dc15ad6469" :answer/id #uuid "3bda799f-2dc1-508a-b332-a2dc15ad6469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-5t}-4{e}^{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbd12f7d-a1de-5498-8a07-57a3b71dfca4" :answer/id #uuid "bbd12f7d-a1de-5498-8a07-57a3b71dfca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{e}^{-5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-227e8665-3923-5e3b-9f94-01de1d340546" :activity/id #uuid "227e8665-3923-5e3b-9f94-01de1d340546" :activity/title "Second-Order Homogeneous ODEs: Characteristic Equations With Distinct Real Roots" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048391 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-2c217041-6e07-5b2b-ab0b-44e2beb8265c" "step-b72723e4-6cca-52eb-af62-fa6496045372" "step-90c0dd24-f5ff-5d53-a9db-2ea11550684f"] :activity/first-step "step-2c217041-6e07-5b2b-ab0b-44e2beb8265c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c217041-6e07-5b2b-ab0b-44e2beb8265c" :step/id #uuid "2c217041-6e07-5b2b-ab0b-44e2beb8265c" :step/content 17592186079206 :step/next "step-b72723e4-6cca-52eb-af62-fa6496045372" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b72723e4-6cca-52eb-af62-fa6496045372" :step/id #uuid "b72723e4-6cca-52eb-af62-fa6496045372" :s